WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.668
-My first guest is a
very talented actor.

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.905
He stars in
"Space Jam: A New Legacy,"

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.942
which hits theaters and
HBO Max this Friday.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.177
Please welcome Don Cheadle!

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.446
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.014
Oh, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:18.918
That's -- that's a good man.
Come on, buddy.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.220
Welcome back.
It's so good to see you.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.089
Thank you so much
for doing our show.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.492
And I just want to start off by
saying congratulations

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.694
on getting nominated for
an Emmy, buddy.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.695
Yesterday --

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.163
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:33.599
"Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.335
It only took you
five minutes of screen time,

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:37.837
and you got nominated
for an Emmy.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.907
That's how good you are.
That's how real it is.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.176
-Well, it's like that
concentrated orange juice.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.677
You know,
you just take a tablespoon

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.781
and put it in water
and stir it around.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:51.684
and it's Cheadle, you know.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.520
-Can you tell us anything about
"Armor Wars" or --

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.022
'Cause that's coming out soon.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.757
I know you can't, but can you?

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.426
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.461
-Well, we just are actually
trying to figure out

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.564
what it's going to be,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.700
how to figure out a way to,
you know, put you in it,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.468
which I know
you keep texting me about.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:10.603
-Yeah, I just would
love to be --

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.939
I just want to be
in that universe.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:17.310
-Yeah, we'll figure it out.
Stop texting me, please.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.711
-Just throw me
a little bone, something.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.479
That's all I'm asking for.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.483
You know, Don, I follow you on
all the socials and I love you.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:25.552
You're a good follow,
by the way.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.019
Don Cheadle,
if you want to -- Yeah.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:31.925
So, in your Twitter bio,
you're @doncheadle,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.293
but your name above that
you can change.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.896
You changed it to...

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.535
So "Don't Ask Me Any Google
Questions Cheadle."

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:47.073
What is a --
Who asks you Google questions?

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.741
-Everybody.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.510
A lot of people on Twitter
like to ask me Google questions,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.948
like, you know, "Wow,
that movie that you're in --

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.184
when does it come out?"

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:02.655
I'm like, "You can
find that out on Google."

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.324
-Don't make me Google, yeah.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.492
-Please don't make me Google.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:07.827
-You got to come
right to the source.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.028
They're gonna come
right to Don Cheadle

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.262
and be like,
"When does it come out?"

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:11.964
-Yeah. Yeah. Well, yeah.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.466
-I love that you do that
and I love that you have

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.835
a good sense of humor
about all of it.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.803
I will tell you, though,
"No Sudden Move,"

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.573
which is out right now on
HBO Max, streaming --

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.575
if you haven't seen that,
watch Don Cheadle.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.677
It's a masterstroke.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.678
That's my man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.447
Knows how to do it.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.815
You crushed it.
-Thank you man.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.350
-You crushed it.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.352
And I also wanted to say I love
your mustache in that, as well.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.220
You rock a good mustache.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.622
-Yeah, appreciate that.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.225
-I've been growing
facial hair for, you know,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.460
on and off for since I was 18,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.897
so I feel like I finally hit
the sweet spot, you know?

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:48.668
-I want to talk about
"Space Jam: A New Legacy."

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.836
It's so exciting.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.737
You -- I know you're a
big basketball fan.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:54.139
To be in
"Space Jam: A New Legacy,"

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:56.208
what was that like
when you even got the call?

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.411
Did LeBron call you?

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.712
-No, LeBron didn't
call me personally.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.913
-Oh.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:04.150
-But, you know,
we've since, like, you know,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.384
developed a great friendship.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:09.822
And it's really nice to
have a movie do something

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.957
beyond just be, you know,
something that you're in.

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:13.626
We make these
satellite families,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.262
and, often, you know,
we don't see these people again.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.230
But we've kept in touch
pretty consistently,

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.465
and that's been cool.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.834
And we just saw the movie,
and it's really fun.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.269
And I think people
are going to dig it a lot.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.870
It was a very cool experience.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.905
You know,
it's what you would imagine

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:28.741
being in that fantastical world

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.175
with all those
animated characters,

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:31.978
and then you look over
and there's King James.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.145
So it was kind of wild
but a lot of fun.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.549
-Yeah. Your character is
Al G. Rhythm.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.583
-Correct.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:41.987
-Is it fair to say
he's a villain?

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.223
-You know, I think we're
throwing these words around --

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:49.962
villain, bad guy, misanthrope --
really liberally, you know?

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:53.266
I mean, I think he's a
misunderstood algorithm.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.435
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:57.737
-That is the first time that
anyone's ever called it that.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.172
Yeah, he's a
misunderstood algorithm, yeah.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.274
I guess so, yeah.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.776
He doesn't consider himself
a villain.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.377
-What villains do?

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:06.812
I mean, you've interviewed
some of them.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:10.282
They rarely do.

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:12.484
-You've played basketball with
a bunch of famous people

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:13.720
over the years.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.921
We've talked about some of them.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:19.425
Who is surprisingly
a dirty player?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.795
-I won't go
all the way to "dirty,"

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:28.901
but Adam Sandler
does like to throw his

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.569
girth around somewhat.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:33.139
-What?! "Sandman"?
-Yeah.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:36.142
Sandman likes to, like, get in
the low post and kind of --

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.476
you know, kind of

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:41.814
booty and back and bounce and
a little chicken wing.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.549
You know.
-Yeah.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.550
Chicken wing.
-He's old school.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.951
He's old school.

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.020
He's old school, when that
kind of stuff wasn't illegal,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.021
you know?

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.321
-Yeah.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.791
What was playing with Obama
like? President Obama.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:55.494
-That was a lot of fun.
It was great.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:58.697
He was not on my team,
so I was playing against him,

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:02.067
which was also good, because I
really wanted to beat him.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:06.272
But the person on my team
that was guarding him

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:09.875
didn't really
put it on him kind of like,

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.177
you know, you want someone to
in a basketball game.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.146
I'm like, "Look,
I know he's the president

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:15.748
and I know the
Secret Service is right there

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.783
and will probably kill you
if you hurt him,

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.253
but you have to play hard.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.421
He's a competitor.

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.788
He doesn't want you to
take it easy on him,

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.757
so guard this dude."

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.060
And he just kept
letting him go around him.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.293
And he's like,
"He's the president."

00:05:28.293 --> 00:05:29.762
I was like, "Look,
do you want me to take him?"

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.198
He's like, "No, I'll take him."
I'm like, "Then take him."

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:37.970
So, he went around him one time,
and I said, "Look, foul him."

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:41.406
And the president
looked at me and he said,

00:05:41.406 --> 00:05:43.208
"Did you just say, 'Foul him'?"

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.378
And I said, "Yes.
Yes, Mr. President."

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:48.314
-I love that you called it out.
"Foul the president."

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.316
Yeah, come on, play ball.
-Foul this dude.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.952
-Yeah, he would respect you
more if you played.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.421
-Exactly.
-That's exactly right.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:58.757
Well, I'm psyched about
"Space Jam: A New Legacy."

00:05:58.757 --> 00:06:00.726
I'm so happy every time
you come on the show.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.027
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:04.163
Here's Don Cheadle
and LeBron James in

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.566
"Space Jam: A New Legacy,"
out this Friday.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.566
Take a look.

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.401
-We're in the computer.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:10.903
-We're in the computer?!
-Dad...

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:11.904
-You know I'm claustrophobic.
-Dad...

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:12.938
-How do we get out of here?

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:14.106
-Dad...
-Where's the elevators?

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:15.741
Hey, Siri, can you let us
out of here, please?

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:16.743
-Siri?
-Who's goes there?

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.943
-Aah!

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:22.515
-Who dares disturb the
great and powerful Al G.?

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.219
[ Laughs ]
Look at your faces.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:29.488
You were terrified! "Aah!"

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:31.691
[ Laughs ] Priceless!

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:40.266
♪♪

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.501
See? Nothing to be afraid of.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.837
-That's right --
nothing to be afraid of.

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:47.639
Don Cheadle, the one and only.

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:50.609
Don Cheadle,
"Space Jam: A New Legacy"

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:55.081
is in theaters and streaming on
HBO Max starting Friday.

